{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "b724ea74-d5d7-4928-9cd1-7a7850e4e179"/*SampleCurve*/,
  "Description": "Samples an editable curve at position U and outputs the value.\n\nThe curve is edited directly in the operator's graph node or in the Parameter window, the same way as animation curves in the timeline. The curve itself is also available as an output, e.g. for [CurvesToTexture].\n\nTips:\n- Click to select points, drag to move points and their tangents.\n- Alt+click on the curve to add a point.\n- Right-click for options like interpolation; right-drag to pan the view.\n- The icon in the upper left corner opens the curve in a bigger window.\n- Connect [AnimValue] to U to get an easily editable animated curve.\n- Selecting and moving the operator in the graph is easiest by dragging the area to the left of the curve editor.\n\nSee also: [AnimValue], [Sin]",
  "SymbolTags": "8",
  "InputUis": [
    {
      "InputId": "108cb829-5f9e-4a45-bc6b-7cf40a0a0f89"/*Curve*/,
